# CODEOWNERS — Uuriko/project-room
#
# Why this exists: several workflows run on `push: branches: [main]`
# (staging.yml, test.yml, machine.yml, relay.yml, ...) and staging.yml
# passes deploy secrets (CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID,
# ROOM_AGENT_CARD_SIGNING_KEY) into those post-merge runs. With reviews
# advisory, a PR that rewrites a workflow file could merge and then
# exfiltrate secrets on the next main push. So workflow changes need the
# owner's explicit review.
#
# This file only takes effect once the branch-protection rule for `main`
# enables "Require review from Code Owners" (admin setting, one click:
# repo Settings → Branches → main rule → check the box). Until then these
# entries are advisory, like all other reviews in this repo.
#
# Action `uses:` refs in this repo are already SHA-pinned; this file is the
# remaining half of the workflow-integrity fix.

# Workflow definitions: owner review required.
.github/workflows/ @Uuriko

# This file itself: don't let a PR quietly drop the gate.
.github/CODEOWNERS @Uuriko
